+  "lastEditedBy": "user://39bd872b-594c-8119-a5d3-0002278b998d",
+  "content": "The Golden Quantum Framework is a paradigm-shifting computational architecture that evolved from substrate-agnostic mathematical quantum simulations into a transfinite, hardware-free reality engine.\n\n\\&lt;heading&gt;Phase 1: Substrate-Agnostic Mathematical Quantum Computing\\&lt;/heading&gt;&lt;br /&gt;The framework began with the assertion that quantum computation does not require physical qubits. By utilizing double-precision complex number matrices (Mathematical Hamiltonian Engine) and pure mathematical oracles, quantum superposition and interference were simulated with infinite coherence time, removing the need for exothermal physical hardware.\n\n\\&lt;heading&gt;Phase 2: Golden Ratio Scaling and Convergence\\&lt;/heading&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Moving beyond standard Grover limits, the framework incorporated the Golden Ratio (φ) as its core evolutionary constant. Dynamic Phase Amplitude Feedback Loops applied synthetic phase biases to accelerate interference convergence. The use of φ prevented discrete periodic recurrence and enabled optimal non-linear amplitude amplification.\n\n\\&lt;heading&gt;Phase 3: Transfinite Memory and The Infinity Fold\\&lt;/heading&gt;&lt;br /&gt;To overcome finite RAM limitations, the framework mapped indices into the &lt;b&gt;Prime Gap Addressing Space&lt;/b&gt;. By treating the empty mathematical spaces between prime numbers as a computational substrate, the framework achieved infinite memory capacity (The Void-Drive) with zero physical memory allocation, allowing searches beyond 2\\^100 states.\n\n## Phase 4: Super-GPU Composition and Attested Compute Fabric\n\nThe repository implements the &lt;b&gt;Infinity GPU&lt;/b&gt; concept as &lt;code&gt;SuperGPU&lt;/code&gt;: a virtual device assembled from the hardware and execution backends that are actually detected on the host. &lt;code&gt;ClusterInventory&lt;/code&gt; records available CPU, iGPU, GPU, ASIC/MMIO, and RTL-design capabilities; &lt;code&gt;SuperGPU&lt;/code&gt; then routes each operation only to a device with the required measured capability. OpenCL is the primary portable GPU execution path, with explicit CPU/NumPy or &lt;code&gt;hashlib&lt;/code&gt; fallback when no compatible GPU is available.\n\nFor mining, SHA-256d nonce windows can be partitioned into disjoint ranges across runnable devices using measured hashrate when available, otherwise compute-unit weighting. Every device-reported candidate is rechecked by the host with &lt;code&gt;hashlib&lt;/code&gt;; the protocol target remains the sole acceptance authority. The unified-punch layer executes its classical kernels on an available OpenCL device and reports the real backend and device rather than presenting CPU fallback as GPU execution.\n\nThe Lucas/Pisot ladder configures search dimensions, chunk sizes, workgroup sizes, and routing metadata. It is a scheduling and scaling discipline—not a substitute for executed hashes. Each dispatch can emit an attestation containing the operation, backend, device, capability used, Lucas rung, workload partition, measured duration, clock source, and truth class.\n\nThe implemented &lt;b&gt;compute fabric&lt;/b&gt; therefore coordinates capability discovery, routing, partitioning, execution, verification, and telemetry. It does not eliminate physical transmission or latency. Only executed dispatch timings, verified hashes, and pool-accepted shares qualify as measured performance; projected Lucas-scaled figures remain explicitly marked as unmeasured.\n\n\\&lt;heading&gt;Phase 5: Mandelbrot Convergence and Fractal Tuning\\&lt;/heading&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Phase noise and floating-point drift were eradicated by anchoring search vectors to the boundary of the Mandelbrot set. This Fractal Resonance Engine snaps vectors to nearest fractal edges, providing superconducting logic without physical cooling.\n\n\\&lt;heading&gt;Phase 6: The Universal Constant Interface (UCI)\\&lt;/heading&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Ascending to the Mathematical Universe Hypothesis, the framework introduced the UCI. By treating physical constants (like the speed of light &lt;i&gt;c&lt;/i&gt;, Planck's constant &lt;i&gt;h&lt;/i&gt;, and the fine structure constant &lt;i&gt;α&lt;/i&gt;) as mutable kernel variables, the framework transitions from running algorithms to directly \"manifesting\" results by manipulating the root reality substrate.\n\n&lt;page url=\"https://app.notion.com/p/c79745a4c61e4210933751d9931e1f65\"&gt;\nGolden Quantum — Research Advancement &amp; Institutional Validation Roadmap\n&lt;/page&gt;",
